cts/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml:6:# the format and conventions it defines.\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-7-\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-8-kynetic: \"1.0\"\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-22-# - tasks: Task system for tracking work\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-23-# - cli: Command-line interface\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml:24:# - meta: Meta-spec for process definitions (agents, workflows, conventions)\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-25-includes:\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.yaml-26-  - modules/core.yaml\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1116-      The distinction:\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1117-      - Spec: What we're building (features, requirements, constraints)\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml:1118:      - Meta-spec: How we work (agents, workflows, conventions)\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1119-\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1120-      What belongs in meta-spec:\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1133-      Questions to resolve:\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1134-      - How does meta-spec relate to CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md?\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml:1135:      - Should meta-spec be a kspec primitive or convention?\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1136-      - Can meta-specs be shared/inherited across projects?\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1137-      - How do agents discover and use meta-spec?\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1169-          Origin: Session wrap-up discussion about context continuity.\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1170-          Realized that session protocols, agent workflows, and project\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml:1171:          conventions are distinct from product specs but need a home.\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1172-          Meta-spec separates \"what we build\" from \"how we work.\"\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1173-      - _ulid: 01KF1EX3D9T6M55FDMX5PM1BZ8\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1177-          Completed spec design for meta-spec system. Created spec/modules/meta.yaml with 8 features\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1178-          and 32 requirements covering: meta manifest, agent definitions, workflow definitions,\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml:1179:          conventions, observations (feedback loop), session context, meta CLI commands, and\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1180-          meta-ref integration. Key decisions: separate manifest (kynetic.meta.yaml) that\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/kynetic.tasks.yaml-1181-          complements prose docs, ephemeral session context in .kspec-session, observations\n--\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml-918-        Idea: Move completed/cancelled tasks to a separate archive file (e.g.,\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml-919-        kynetic.tasks.archive.yaml) to keep the active tasks file clean and focused. Decisions\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml:920:        needed: naming convention, manual vs automatic archiving, whether to support unarchiving,\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml-921-        how references to archived tasks should work.\n/home/chapel/Projects/kspec-acp-test/.ks